<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Judaea</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Judaea was the region of the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a> centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>, the land of the Jewish people in antiquity. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a> its Jewish communities initially kept their ancestral law. The attempted suppression of Jewish practice by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antiochus-iv-epiphanes">Antiochus IV</a> triggered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maccabean-revolt">Maccabean revolt</a> in Judaea.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/judaea.jpg" alt="Judaea" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Davidbena · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Giv%27at_Seled,_near_Tzafririm.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
